=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
**Affected component:** The Apache2 HTTP web server daemon on srv1 (10.5.0.4).

**Mechanism:** srv1 hosts two services: BIND (`named`) as the campus DNS authority for `jeremysitlab.com`, and Apache2 as the web server. `named` is running and healthy — it correctly resolves `srv1.jeremysitlab.com → 10.5.0.4` and all three campus clients use `10.5.0.4` as their nameserver. However, Apache2 has stopped; `ps aux` on srv1 shows only `bash` (PID 1) and `named` (PID 30) — no web server process at all, and `ss -tlnp` confirms nothing is listening on port 80. When clients connect to `http://srv1.jeremysitlab.com/`, DNS resolves the name correctly, but the TCP connection to port 80 is immediately refused (curl code 000, ~3 ms). This connection refusal is what users experience as "not found" in their browsers — it is **not** a DNS failure.

**Localization:** srv1 exclusively. All L2/L3 paths are healthy (0% packet loss confirmed), OSPF fabric is stable across all distribution and core switches, and DNS (`named`) on srv1 is fully operational.

**Root cause:** The Apache2 web server daemon has crashed or been stopped on srv1, leaving port 80 without a listener while the DNS service continues to run normally.

**Fix:** Restart Apache2 on srv1: `service apache2 start` (or `apache2ctl start`). Investigate `/var/log/apache2/error.log` on srv1 to determine why it crashed — the user notes this has happened before ("again"), suggesting a recurring application-level issue.
=== END ===